  "id": "ipsilateral-eye",
  "term": "ipsilateral eye",
  "definition": "The ipsilateral eye is the eye on the same side as the brain area being discussed. In this source, it refers to eye input that can activate parts of the visual wulst and can also influence responses driven by the opposite eye.",
